# Error Handling Rules

## Error Mapping Convention

All technical errors must be mapped to user-friendly messages before showing to users.

### Standard Error Mapping Function

```dart
String _mapError(dynamic error) {
  if (error is PostgrestException) {
    switch (error.code) {
      case '42501': // RLS denied
        return 'Session expired. Please log in again.';
      case '23505': // Unique violation
        return 'This item already exists.';
      case '23503': // Foreign key violation
        return 'Related item does not exist.';
      case '23514': // Check constraint violation
        return 'Invalid data provided.';
      case '22P02': // Invalid input syntax (UUID, etc.)
        return 'Invalid identifier provided.';
      default:
        return 'Database error occurred. Please try again.';
    }
  }
  
  if (error is AuthException) {
    if (error.message.contains('Invalid login credentials')) {
      return 'Email or password is incorrect.';
    }
    if (error.message.contains('Email already registered')) {
      return 'An account with this email already exists.';
    }
    return 'Authentication error. Please try again.';
  }
  
  if (error is StorageException) {
    if (error.statusCode == 404) {
      return 'File not available.';
    }
    return 'Upload failed. Please try again.';
  }
  
  if (error is SocketException || error is TimeoutException) {
    return 'Cannot reach the server. Check your connection and retry.';
  }
  
  // Fallback
  return 'An error occurred. Please try again.';
}
```

## Common Error Codes

### Database Errors (PostgrestException)

| Code | Meaning | User Message |
|------|---------|--------------|
| `42501` | RLS denied | "Session expired. Please log in again." |
| `23505` | Unique violation | "This item already exists." |
| `23503` | Foreign key violation | "Related item does not exist." |
| `23514` | Check constraint violation | "Invalid data provided." |
| `22P02` | Invalid input syntax | "Invalid identifier provided." |
| `42P01` | Table does not exist | "Service unavailable. Please contact support." |

### Auth Errors (AuthException)

| Error | User Message |
|-------|--------------|
| Invalid login credentials | "Email or password is incorrect." |
| Email already registered | "An account with this email already exists." |
| Weak password | "Password is too weak. Use at least 8 characters." |
| Invalid email | "Please enter a valid email address." |

### Storage Errors (StorageException)

| Status Code | User Message |
|-------------|--------------|
| 404 | "File not available." |
| 413 | "File is too large. Please choose a smaller file." |
| 400 | "Invalid file type. Please choose a different file." |

### Network Errors

| Error Type | User Message |
|------------|--------------|
| SocketException | "Cannot reach the server. Check your connection and retry." |
| TimeoutException | "Request timed out. Please try again." |
| HttpException | "Network error occurred. Please try again." |

## ViewModel Error Handling Pattern

```dart
class ExampleViewModel extends ChangeNotifier {
  String? _error;
  bool _isLoading = false;
  
  String? get error => _error;
  bool get isLoading => _isLoading;
  
  Future<void> performAction() async {
    _isLoading = true;
    _error = null;
    notifyListeners();
    
    try {
      await _service.performAction();
      AppLogger.i('Action completed successfully');
    } catch (e) {
      _error = _mapError(e);
      AppLogger.e('Action failed', e);
    } finally {
      _isLoading = false;
      notifyListeners();
    }
  }
  
  String _mapError(dynamic e) {
    // Use standard error mapping function
    // ...
  }
  
  void clearError() {
    _error = null;
    notifyListeners();
  }
}
```

## UI Error Display

### SnackBar Pattern

```dart
// In ViewModel
void _showError(String message) {
  // Store error in ViewModel
  _error = message;
  notifyListeners();
}

// In View
Consumer<ExampleViewModel>(
  builder: (context, viewModel, child) {
    if (viewModel.error != null) {
      WidgetsBinding.instance.addPostFrameCallback((_) {
        ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
          SnackBar(
            content: Text(viewModel.error!),
            backgroundColor: AppColors.lightRed,
            action: SnackBarAction(
              label: 'Dismiss',
              onPressed: () => viewModel.clearError(),
            ),
          ),
        );
      });
    }
    return YourWidget();
  },
)
```

### Error Widget Pattern

```dart
if (viewModel.error != null)
  Container(
    padding: const EdgeInsets.all(AppDimens.p16),
    color: AppColors.lightRed.withValues(alpha: 0.1),
    child: Row(
      children: [
        Icon(Icons.error_outline, color: AppColors.lightRed),
        SizedBox(width: AppDimens.p8),
        Expanded(
          child: Text(
            viewModel.error!,
            style: AppTypography.body.copyWith(
              color: AppColors.lightRed,
            ),
          ),
        ),
        IconButton(
          icon: Icon(Icons.close),
          onPressed: () => viewModel.clearError(),
        ),
      ],
    ),
  )
```

## RLS Error Handling

RLS errors (42501) typically mean:
1. User session expired
2. User doesn't have permission
3. Invalid user context

**Always handle RLS errors gracefully**:

```dart
try {
  await supabase.from('profiles').select().eq('id', userId);
} on PostgrestException catch (e) {
  if (e.code == '42501') {
    // Session expired - redirect to login
    Navigator.pushReplacementNamed(context, '/login');
    return;
  }
  rethrow;
}
```

## Logging Errors

Always log errors with context:

```dart
try {
  await _service.performAction();
} catch (e, stackTrace) {
  AppLogger.e(
    'Failed to perform action: userId=$userId, action=$actionName',
    e,
    stackTrace,
  );
  _error = _mapError(e);
}
```

**Important**: Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, etc.)

## Error Recovery

### Retry Pattern

```dart
Future<T> retryOperation<T>(
  Future<T> Function() operation, {
  int maxRetries = 3,
  Duration delay = const Duration(seconds: 1),
}) async {
  for (int i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++) {
    try {
      return await operation();
    } catch (e) {
      if (i == maxRetries - 1) rethrow;
      await Future.delayed(delay * (i + 1));
    }
  }
  throw Exception('Max retries exceeded');
}
```

### Offline Handling

```dart
try {
  await _service.syncData();
} on SocketException catch (e) {
  // Store for later sync
  await _localStorage.savePendingSync(data);
  _error = 'No internet connection. Data will sync when online.';
}
```

